# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 📦 **Packaging ignore — core fragment (universal)**
# Excluded for every extension of every ecosystem: editor and operating-system state, repository documentation beyond the marketplace pair, governance surfaces, and packaging residue. The whole file is the governed region; composition is pinned by the canonical verifier through byte identity.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# .vscode/** — workspace editor state; local machine material, never runtime content.
.vscode/**
# .idea/** — JetBrains project state; personal editor data.
.idea/**
# .DS_Store — Finder metadata; operating-system droppings.
.DS_Store
# *.log — local log residue; never meaningful on a user machine.
*.log
# tmp/** — scratch trees; regenerable, meaningless in a package.
tmp/**
# .cache/** — tool cache trees; local-only state.
.cache/**
# docs/** — repository documentation; the marketplace renders README and CHANGELOG only.
docs/**
# CONTRIBUTING.md — contributor guidance; repository material, not runtime content.
CONTRIBUTING.md
# .github/** — platform automation; runs before packaging exists.
.github/**
# repo-bindings.json — the governance declaration; consumed by the verifier, never at runtime.
repo-bindings.json
# git-governance.quality.json — the configuration seam; governance-time input only.
git-governance.quality.json
# license.values.json — the license render input; governance-time input only.
license.values.json
# license.lock.json — the license render pin; governance-time input only.
license.lock.json
# lefthook.yml — the local hook contract; development-environment surface.
lefthook.yml
# .vscodeignore — the packaging contract itself; inert inside the package.
.vscodeignore
# .gitignore — the version-control contract; inert inside the package.
.gitignore
# .gitattributes — the attribute contract; inert inside the package.
.gitattributes
# dist/vsix/** — the vsix staging tree; a package must never contain a package.
dist/vsix/**
# *.vsix — built packages; distribution residue inside the repository.
*.vsix
# **/*.map — source maps; they disclose original paths, names, and source text (source-map rule).
**/*.map
